      "tag": "Square",
      "h2": "cis/trans in square planar",
      "body_html": "<p>For [Pt(NH3)2Cl2]: cis has both NH3 adjacent (90 deg); trans has NH3 opposite (180 deg).</p><p>cis-platin binds DNA between adjacent guanines to halt cell division (cancer therapy). Trans isomer inactive.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Oct",
      "h2": "cis/trans in octahedral",
      "body_html": "<p>[Co(NH3)4Cl2]+: two Cl can be cis (90 deg) or trans (180 deg). Cis isomer is purple; trans is green.</p><p>cis form often optically active if it lacks a mirror plane.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Optical",
      "h2": "Optical isomers in TM complexes",
      "body_html": "<p>Three bidentate ligands around an octahedral centre (e.g. [Co(en)3]^3+) make a non-superimposable mirror pair.</p><p>Detected by rotation of plane-polarised light (Λ and Δ enantiomers).</p>"
    }
